# Licensing

CanILiveThere is published under two licences, because it is two
different kinds of work in one repository. Both require the same thing of
you: **credit us.** Neither asks you to pay, ask permission, or keep
anything closed.

Copyright © 2026 CanILiveThere.

---

## 1. Content and data — CC BY 4.0

**Applies to:** everything in `derived/`, the prose in `l/`, and the
written copy across the site — the country and location facts, the
sourcing, the verdicts, the criteria, the portraits.

Licensed under the [Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
Licence (CC BY 4.0)](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

You may copy it, republish it, reshape it, build a product on it, and
charge for that product. The single condition is **attribution**: say
where it came from, and link back.

CC BY 4.0 is used deliberately rather than a hand-written licence.
Version 4.0 explicitly licenses **sui generis database rights** as well
as copyright — which matters here, because facts themselves are not
copyrightable in most jurisdictions. What has value in this project is
not any individual sentence; it is the verified collection. Database
right is the instrument that protects investment in obtaining and
verifying a collection, and 4.0 is the version that covers it.

**How to attribute** — copy this:

> Data from [CanILiveThere](https://canilivethere.info), licensed
> [CC BY 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

If you changed it, say so. Do not imply we endorse you or checked your
version.

